\tag{fdip}
\title{Discrete induction and its open interfaces}
\date{2026-10-30}

\p{A finite Gaussian model already distinguishes an induced
interaction from a supplied one: [integrating fields creates new
couplings](fdip-000F) among the retained fields. The larger question is which
algebraic and geometric structures can organize such induction,
background variation and a controlled continuum comparison.}

\p{The [synthesis conjecture](fdip-003X) states that broader target.
The [finite interfaces](fdip-003Y) begin with an exact retained
expectation and distinguish the structures it constructs from the
additional maps the conjecture would require.}

\transclude{fdip-003X}
\transclude{fdip-003Y}
